  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-301304-102</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Institutional Reforms Programme - Implementation through UNDP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention will work at the core of government, reinforcing critical governance mechanisms at federal level. It will strengthen the institutions mandated to coordinate between the federal and provincial levels of government, allocate and distribute resources between them in an equitable manner, and will improve coordination between ministries including for anticipating and responding to crises.  It will also explore supporting the Parliament exercise its oversight better. The proposed intervention is mostly geared towards addressing &#x201c;how&#x201d; the institutions of governance work rather than &#x201c;what&#x201d; they are working on. The intervention is non-sectoral, but it is expected to have visible results in critical areas such as the ability of the government to continue to successfully steer the country through the ongoing crises, and in sectors relevant to UK&#x2019;s priorities in Pakistan, such as population dynamics, the economy and work on climate adaptation and resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
